⭐ IMPORTANT OBSERVATION
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

nums1 ke elements, nums2 ke subset hote hain.

Isliye:

    nums2 me NGE calculate once

then:

    nums1 → O(1) average lookup


This is MUCH better than:

For every nums1 element:
    nums2 me search karo
    aur right side scan karo


━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
⚠️ WHY MONOTONIC STACK?
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

Brute Force:

For every element:
    right side ke elements check karo
    jab tak greater na mil jaye.

Worst case:

    O(n²)


Monotonic Stack:

    Each element → push once
    Each element → pop at most once

Therefore:

    O(n)


This is the main optimization.


━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
🧩 STACK ME VALUE YA INDEX?
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

Is problem me:

    stack<int> st;

me VALUE store karna sufficient hai.

Because answer directly:
    next greater VALUE

chahiye.


Daily Temperatures me:

    stack INDEX

store kiya tha because hume:

    "kitne days baad?"

calculate karna tha.

So remember:

    NGE value chahiye
        → values store kar sakte ho

    Distance/index chahiye
        → indices store karo


